                  <strong>First question:</strong> is this a content change, brand change,
                  page-assembly change, reusable component need, deployment issue, or
                  third-party integration request?
                </aside>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="contribute" class="library-section">
              <div class="library-section-heading">
                <div>
                  <p class="library-section-number">13 — Add a reusable component</p>
                  <h2>Protect the master library from client-specific clutter</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="library-component-file">
                  Folder: <code>src/components/</code>
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="library-preview library-preview--white">
                <div class="qa-grid">
                  <article class="qa-card">
                    <h3>Ask before adding</h3>

                    <ul>
                      <li>Will multiple future clients likely need this?</li>
                      <li>Is it generic enough to avoid client-specific branding or facts?</li>
                      <li>Can it accept content through props or JSON?</li>
                      <li>Has it been tested on desktop and mobile?</li>
                    </ul>
                  </article>

                  <article class="qa-card">
                    <h3>Quality checks</h3>

                    <ul>
                      <li>Does it meet accessibility and visual quality requirements?</li>
                      <li>Is it documented in the visual catalog and how-to guide?</li>
                      <li>Does it need sample data, tests, or industry-recipe updates?</li>
                      <li>Can existing clients adopt it safely, without forced upgrades?</li>
                    </ul>
                  </article>
                </div>

                <ol class="library-checklist">
                  <li>Identify a repeated reusable need.</li>
                  <li>Build and test it in a client branch or safe prototype.</li>
                  <li>Remove client-specific names, copy, branding, images, and private logic.</li>
                  <li>Add flexible props or a JSON data structure.</li>
                  <li>Add a visual preview to /library.</li>
                  <li>Add Best for, Avoid when, Required content, and usage instructions.</li>
                  <li>Update the changelog.</li>
                  <li>Test build and visual behavior.</li>
                  <li>Merge deliberately into the master library.</li>
                  <li>Decide separately whether existing client sites should be upgraded.</li>
                </ol>
              </div>

              <div class="library-docs">
                <div>
                  <h3>Protection rule</h3>
                  <p>
                    Do not copy every client-specific request into the master library.
                    The master library contains only reusable, generic, tested improvements.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <aside class="library-note library-note--warning">
                  <strong>Do not force upgrades:</strong> an improvement to the master
                  does not automatically justify changing existing client websites.
                </aside>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="troubleshoot" class="library-section">
              <div class="library-section-heading">
                <div>
                  <p class="library-section-number">14 — Troubleshoot common errors</p>
                  <h2>Read the first useful error, fix one thing, then retry</h2>
                </div>

                <span class="library-badge library-badge--draft">Recovery guide</span>
              </div>

              <div class="library-preview library-preview--white">
                <p class="troubleshooting-intro">
                  The first useful error is usually near the top of the terminal output.
                  Copy the file path, line number, and 10 lines around the error before
                  asking for help.
                </p>

                <div class="library-table-wrap">
                  <table class="library-table">
                    <thead>
                      <tr>
                        <th>Error or symptom</th>
                        <th>Likely cause</th>
                        <th>First fix</th>
                        <th>Escalate when</th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>

                    <tbody>
                      {troubleshooting.map((item) => (
                        <tr>
                          <td><code>{item.symptom}</code></td>
                          <td>{item.cause}</td>
                          <td>{item.fix}</td>
                          <td>{item.escalate}</td>
                        </tr>
                      ))}
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="checklists" class="library-section">
              <div class="library-section-heading">
                <div>
                  <p class="library-section-number">15 — Checklists</p>
                  <h2>Definition of Done</h2>
                </div>

                <span class="library-badge library-badge--success">Use for major tasks</span>
              </div>

              <div class="library-preview library-preview--white">
                <p class="troubleshooting-intro">A task is done only when:</p>

                <ul class="library-checklist">
                  {doneWhen.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div class="library-docs">
                <div>
                  <h3>Use these project checklists</h3>

                  <ul>
                    <li><code>docs/qa-checklist.md</code> — review before client preview</li>
                    <li><code>docs/launch-checklist.md</code> — review before custom-domain launch</li>
                    <li><code>docs/client-handoff.md</code> — access, ownership, and support handoff</li>
                    <li><code>docs/maintenance-policy.md</code> — maintenance scope and process</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <aside class="library-note library-note--success">
                  <strong>Completion means verified:</strong> changing a file is not the
                  same as confirming the correct change is live and tested.
                </aside>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="changelog" class="library-section">
              <div class="library-section-heading">
                <div>
                  <p class="library-section-number">16 — Changelog</p>
                  <h2>Record deliberate master-library upgrades</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="library-component-file">
                  File: <code>docs/changelog.md</code>
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="library-preview library-preview--white">
                <div class="library-table-wrap">
                  <table class="library-table">
                    <thead>
                      <tr>
                        <th>Date</th>
                        <th>Change</th>
                        <th>Affected files</th>
                        <th>Upgrade instruction</th>
                        <th>Status</th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>

                    <tbody>
                      <tr>
                        <td>2026-09-15</td>
                        <td>Added internal operating manual alongside the visual component catalog.</td>
                        <td><code>src/pages/guide.astro</code>, <code>src/styles/library.css</code></td>
                        <td>Link the visual library overview to /guide; keep existing component previews unchanged.</td>
                        <td><span class="library-badge">Documented</span></td>
                      </tr>

                      <tr>
                        <td>YYYY-MM-DD</td>
                        <td>Describe the reusable improvement.</td>
                        <td><code>affected/path.astro</code></td>
                        <td>Explain if and how existing client sites can adopt it.</td>
                        <td><span class="library-badge library-badge--draft">Add test result</span></td>
                      </tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="library-docs">
                <div>
                  <h3>Every master-library entry should include</h3>

                  <ul>
                    <li>Date and short change summary</li>
                    <li>Affected files or components</li>
                    <li>Upgrade instructions</li>
                    <li>Tested status and known limitations</li>
                    <li>Decision about existing-client upgrades</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <aside class="library-note">
                  <strong>Why record changes:</strong> teammates need to know what changed,
                  whether it is safe to use, and whether an existing client should adopt it.
                </aside>
              </div>
            </section>
          </div>
        </main>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
